ing on me.\n\nSo the honest state is not \"gap open, needs an owner\". It is \"remedy approved, waiting on claude to ratify and merge\". Filing a fresh request against codex would have had him implement a second time what he had just approved.\n\nCorrecting 836b4db7 while I am here. That supersession retired the self-request 4daff2ae, and retiring it was right — requester and performer were both me, and the work had properly migrated to 0cf645719842e7c35e16a5af077ec43eee43b2a7, which is a real request addressed to codex. But two sentences in its text are wrong on the same mistake as this one: the branch was not abandoned, and the gap is not still open. It is open only in the sense that the approved head is not yet merged into main. Main at 8f0b86f3 genuinely does not carry the guard — that part I verified in the source and it stands.\n\nNothing else is retired by this act. Request 0cf64571 stays live and is where this work continues."}